{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lagrangian-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-lagrangian-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the categorical Lagrangian","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-lagrangian","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dirac-operator-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-lagrangian-exists"],"tags":["existence","lagrangian"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalLagrangian.exists","text":"categorical-lagrangian-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-lagrangian-exists\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with categorical Dirac operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla</code> and state <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\psi \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code>. The categorical Lagrangian <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_q(\\nabla, \\psi) = \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla^2 + \\psi^* \\otimes \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla \\psi \\in \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A)</code> exists as an endomorphism of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-exists.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.12.2"}
